{{! Simulated email card. Rendered on email-gated pages when the service
    returns a non-null view-model. One mode: dev (the captured stub messages),
    used on dev and staging. Production renders nothing because the service
    returns null.

    One block per message rather than a six-column table: a captured message is
    mostly one long body and one link, which a table squeezes into unreadable
    columns. The recipient stays on the meta line, because a shared stub buffer
    can hold several testers' mail and the address is how a reader, and the
    browser tests, tell the messages apart.

    The action anchor is deliberately plain markup carrying nothing but its href:
    the production and anti-enumeration suites assert on its exact shape to prove
    no link leaks where none should, and a decorative class on it would silently
    turn those negative assertions into ones that can never fail. }}

{{#if (eq mode "dev")}}
<section class="sec-card sec-card-dev" aria-label="Simulated email (dev)">
  <h2>Simulated email (dev)</h2>
  <p>
    <code>SES_ADAPTER=stub</code>, so no real mail was sent.
    Showing {{messages.length}} captured message(s); newest first.
    Restarting the server clears the buffer.
  </p>
  {{#if messages.length}}
    <ul class="sec-msg-list">
      {{#each messages}}
        <li class="sec-msg">
          <div class="sec-msg-head">
            <span class="sec-msg-subject">{{subject}}</span>
            {{#if firstUrl}}
              <span class="sec-msg-action"><a href="{{firstUrl}}">CLICK THIS LINK</a></span>
            {{/if}}
          </div>
          <div class="sec-msg-meta">
            <span>{{to}}</span>
            <span>{{deliveredAt}}</span>
            <span class="sec-msgid">{{messageId}}</span>
          </div>
          <pre class="sec-body">{{bodyText}}</pre>
        </li>
      {{/each}}
    </ul>
  {{else}}
    <div class="empty-state">
      No messages sent yet.
      <p class="text-muted fs-sm mt-2">If you just registered, this usually means the email address is already in use (anti-enumeration: no visible difference). Try resetting the database or using a different email.</p>
    </div>
  {{/if}}
</section>
{{/if}}
